  "body": "PR1254 established three crossings but left their number and common safe interval unresolved. All three differences have the same four-term +,-,-,+ shape. A short Rolle argument now proves exactly one interior crossing per pair, and independent rational log/Taylor arithmetic brackets them within 1/1024. The newer profiles have strictly smaller native moments for every 0 < a <= 43/128.\n\nPython 3.12 registered replay passes, with independent square-root signs and four theorem-premise controls. Exact predecessor Git/SHA256 pins, proof, task draw, receipt and structured next question included. Source-bound owner-map admission is inherited; no new supplier root, physical replay or kappa is claimed. Credit mightyOil PR1254 and the retained T16 authors. Substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0.\n\nBase: `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`. [Coordinated research batch](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1163#discussioncomment-18922638); round 14. The selected record is unchanged.\n",
